<BaseLayout title="About MAKHEX | Hardware, Explained" description="ESP32 projects with transparent bills of materials, practical building blocks and community-verifiable guidance.">
<section class="page-hero container"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE ABOUT MAKHEX</span><h1>Less scrolling.<br/><em>More making.</em></h1><div class="page-hero-bottom"><p>Finding a board is easy. Knowing which version will actually work in your build is harder.</p><span class="page-count">Make it · document it · share it</span></div></section>
<section class="section container about-story"><div><span class="eyebrow">WHAT WE BELIEVE</span><h2>A parts list should come with a plan.</h2></div><div><p>MAKHEX is a maker-focused storefront concept starting with ESP32 boards, touch displays, sensors and compatible components. We make it easier to go from “I want to build this” to a clear bill of materials and practical build workflow.</p><p>We're launching in stages. Today the site contains research-stage component candidates and project blueprints. Qualified product pages will add real photos, supplier information, tested compatibility and links to our separate Squarespace checkout.</p><p>Every build is a living document. The community can propose corrections and improvements through GitHub, with proposed and tested information labeled separately.</p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/projects/">FIND YOUR FIRST BUILD ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="container values-grid"><div><span>01 / OPEN</span><h3>SHARE THE WORK</h3><p>Public code and reviewable contributions.</p></div><div><span>02 / HONEST</span><h3>VERIFY BEFORE SELLING</h3><p>Clear supply and compatibility gates.</p></div><div><span>03 / USEFUL</span><h3>BUILDS OVER HYPE</h3><p>A real outcome for each component.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
